# Connect NotebookLM to Antigravity via MCP

Connecting NotebookLM will allow Antigravity to interact with your Notebooks, sources, and notes directly.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> I have identified [C:\Users\Antonio\.gemini\antigravity\mcp_config.json](file:///C:/Users/Antonio/.gemini/antigravity/mcp_config.json) as the likely configuration file. I will populate it with the NotebookLM server settings.
> During the **Authentication** step, a browser window will open. You will need to log in to your Google Account and authorize the application.

## Proposed Changes

### Configuration

#### [MODIFY] [mcp_config.json](file:///C:/Users/Antonio/.gemini/antigravity/mcp_config.json)

Add the `notebooklm` server definition to the `mcpServers` object.

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "notebooklm": {
      "command": "python",
      "args": [
        "-m",
        "notebooklm_mcp_server"
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

## Verification Plan

### Automated Verification
1.  Run `python -m notebooklm_mcp_server.auth --help` to ensure the module is functioning.
2.  After authentication, use the `list_notebooks` tool (via the MCP interface) to verify the connection.

### Manual Verification
1.  **Authentication**: I will run the auth command and provide the URL. You will authorize in the browser.
2.  **Creation**: Create a test notebook or save the current project state to a new notebook using the MCP tools.
